// Hakuro's finer form: what his fitted shapes miss of the sculpted figure the look was drawn
// from (the swell and cut of each muscle, the hollows between), as one smooth function of the
// point, added to his body's distance (`Detail`, a creature `Modifier`).
//
// It's a small network: the point's offset from his middle as 24 waves' phases (each a
// direction and a frequency: Fourier features), their sines and cosines through two layers of
// 32 sines, and a sum. Its numbers were fitted once, offline, to the reference's distance less
// his shapes' (`/mnt/project-files/hakuro-fit/resid.py`), and are written here as source: the
// reference itself never ships. It fades to nothing over his hands, his feet and his head,
// which other pieces make.

use engine::creature::Modifier
use std::derive::{Box3, Interval}

/// The most it moves his surface (m), and the steepest it is (its gradient's length).
pub const MOST: f32 = 0.05
pub const STEEPEST: f32 = 1.8

/// His middle, where the waves' phases are counted from.
const CENTRE = vec3(0.0000, 1.0000, -0.0300)

/// Each wave's direction times its frequency (cycles a metre).
const WAVES: [vec3; 24] = [
    vec3(10.2046, -0.914195, 0.969078),
